# HR360 API Documentation

**Project:** HR360 – Human Resource Management & Analytics System
**Document ID:** HR360-BE-002
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Draft for Review
**Date:** 20 September 2026
**Prepared By:** Nida Khan
**Role:** Business Analyst / Developer / Project Manager / Scrum Master
**Product Owner:** HR Business Stakeholder

---

## 1. Document Purpose

This document defines the REST API interface implemented by the HR360 backend.

It provides a consolidated reference for API modules, endpoint patterns, HTTP methods, business purpose, and implementation status.

---

## 2. API Base URL

Local development base URL:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

All functional APIs use the following structure:

```text
http://localhost:5000/api/<module>
```

---

## 3. API Design Principles

HR360 APIs follow these principles:

* REST-based architecture
* JSON request and response format
* Modular route organization
* PostgreSQL-backed persistence
* HTTP method semantics
* Controlled error responses
* Business-rule validation
* Database integrity enforcement

---

# 4. Employee APIs

## 4.1 Employee Management

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/employees
```

### Retrieve Employees

```text
GET /api/employees
```

Purpose:

Retrieve employee records together with relevant organizational and workforce information.

The response includes information such as:

* Employee ID
* Employee code
* First name
* Last name
* Email
* Phone
* Department
* Job role
* Work status
* Employment status
* Joining date
* Salary amount
* Salary status
* Department-specific active status

---

### Retrieve Employee by ID

```text
GET /api/employees/:id
```

Purpose:

Retrieve a specific employee record.

Example:

```text
GET /api/employees/1
```

---

### Create Employee

```text
POST /api/employees
```

Purpose:

Create a new employee record.

Typical information includes:

```json
{
  "employee_code": "EMP010",
  "first_name": "Example",
  "last_name": "Employee",
  "email": "example@company.com"
}
```

The actual request body must follow the fields supported by the implemented route and database schema.

---

### Update Employee

```text
PUT /api/employees/:id
```

Purpose:

Update employee information.

---

### Update Employee Lifecycle Status

```text
PATCH /api/employees/:id/status
```

Purpose:

Update an employee's lifecycle status.

Supported lifecycle values include:

```text
CANDIDATE
PROBATION
EMPLOYED
ON_LEAVE
RESIGNED
TERMINATED
RETIRED
```

Example request:

```json
{
  "employment_status": "RESIGNED"
}
```

---

### Department-Specific Active Status

The employee API derives:

```text
department_active_status
```

based on the employee's department and applicable HR360 business rule.

---

# 5. Department API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/departments
```

Purpose:

Maintain organizational departments.

The API supports department retrieval and management according to the implemented route.

Example:

```text
GET /api/departments
```

---

# 6. Job Role API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/job-roles
```

Purpose:

Maintain job roles linked to organizational departments.

Example:

```text
GET /api/job-roles
```

---

# 7. Work Status API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/work-statuses
```

Purpose:

Maintain workforce activity statuses.

HR360 work statuses include:

```text
WORKING
ONLINE
TRAINING
ON_BENCH
PIP
ON_LEAVE
OFFLINE
REMOTE
```

Example:

```text
GET /api/work-statuses
```

---

# 8. Attendance API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/attendance
```

Purpose:

Manage employee attendance records.

Attendance statuses include:

```text
PRESENT
ABSENT
LATE
HALF_DAY
ON_LEAVE
HOLIDAY
```

The attendance module supports:

* Recording attendance
* Retrieving attendance records
* Working-hours information

---

# 9. Leave Type API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/leave-types
```

Purpose:

Maintain leave categories and leave policies.

Current leave types include:

```text
Annual Leave
Sick Leave
Casual Leave
Emergency Leave
```

---

# 10. Leave Request API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/leave-requests
```

Purpose:

Manage employee leave requests.

Typical lifecycle:

```text
Submitted
    |
    v
Pending
    |
    +----> Approved
    |
    +----> Rejected
```

The API supports leave request submission and approval/rejection processing.

---

# 11. Performance Review API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/performance-reviews
```

Purpose:

Manage employee performance reviews.

The module supports:

* Creating performance reviews
* Recording ratings
* Retrieving performance history

The current sample performance scale uses ratings such as:

```text
1.00 – 5.00
```

---

# 12. Performance Improvement Plan API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/pips
```

Purpose:

Manage employee Performance Improvement Plans.

PIP information includes:

* Employee
* Start date
* End date
* Status
* Review frequency
* Objectives / review information

Example PIP status:

```text
ACTIVE
```

---

# 13. Training Program API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/training-programs
```

Purpose:

Manage organizational training programs.

Current sample programs include:

* Leadership Development
* Advanced Excel for Business
* Workplace Communication
* Project Management Fundamentals
* Cybersecurity Awareness

---

# 14. Employee Training API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/employee-training
```

Purpose:

Manage employee participation in training programs.

Training participation statuses include:

```text
ENROLLED
ATTENDED
COMPLETED
DID_NOT_ATTEND
CANCELLED
```

The module supports tracking:

* Enrollment
* Attendance
* Completion
* Scores
* Certificate issuance
* Employee feedback

---

# 15. Candidate API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/candidates
```

Purpose:

Manage recruitment candidates.

Candidate lifecycle includes:

```text
NEW
SCREENING
SHORTLISTED
INTERVIEW
OFFERED
HIRED
REJECTED
WITHDRAWN
```

Candidate information includes:

* Candidate code
* Name
* Email
* Phone
* Resume
* Experience
* Qualification
* Current company
* Current designation
* Source
* Status
* Application date

---

# 16. Job Application API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/job-applications
```

Purpose:

Manage candidate applications for job roles.

Application information includes:

* Candidate
* Job role
* Application date
* Application status
* Recruiter
* Expected salary
* Notice period
* Recruiter notes

The database prevents duplicate applications for the same candidate and job role combination.

---

# 17. Interview API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/interviews
```

Purpose:

Manage recruitment interviews.

Interview information includes:

* Application
* Interviewer
* Interview round
* Interview type
* Scheduled date/time
* Interview status
* Rating
* Feedback
* Result

---

# 18. Job Offer API

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/job-offers
```

Purpose:

Manage candidate job offers.

Offer information includes:

* Application
* Offer date
* Joining date
* Offered salary
* Employment type
* Offer status
* Accepted date
* Rejection reason

Offer statuses include:

```text
DRAFT
SENT
ACCEPTED
DECLINED
EXPIRED
CANCELLED
```

---

# 19. Recruitment-to-Employee Transition

The functional requirement for automated transition from an accepted job offer to an employee record is currently:

```text
PLANNED
```

The target process is:

```text
Candidate
    |
    v
Application
    |
    v
Interview
    |
    v
Job Offer
    |
    v
Accepted Offer
    |
    v
Employee Record
```

The automated final transition is not currently implemented.

---

# 20. Analytics APIs

Base endpoint:

```text
/api/analytics
```

The analytics module provides:

| Endpoint                     | Purpose               |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------- |
| `/api/analytics/overview`    | Overall HR metrics    |
| `/api/analytics/departments` | Department analytics  |
| `/api/analytics/attendance`  | Attendance analytics  |
| `/api/analytics/leave`       | Leave analytics       |
| `/api/analytics/performance` | Performance analytics |
| `/api/analytics/training`    | Training analytics    |
| `/api/analytics/recruitment` | Recruitment analytics |

These endpoints provide the backend data layer for future dashboards and Power BI integration.

---

# 21. Health Check API

Endpoint:

```text
GET /api/health
```

Purpose:

Verify backend availability and PostgreSQL connectivity.

Successful response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "HR360 Backend and PostgreSQL are connected",
  "databaseTime": "timestamp"
}
```

